1
00:00:00,956 --> 00:00:04,859
Unlabelled Class D artefacts.
Tosh, I need you to run a full check.

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,661
-Sure.
-JACK: Owen, you can help.

3
00:00:06,762 --> 00:00:09,230
-Happy to.
-Adam, I know how much you love audits.

4
00:00:09,331 --> 00:00:10,565
-It's gotta be done.
-If you could...

5
00:00:10,666 --> 00:00:12,066
Go through the investigation reports,

6
00:00:12,167 --> 00:00:13,768
find out when they might have come
through the rift.

7
00:00:13,869 --> 00:00:16,904
-JACK: You okay with that?
-I have been for the last three years.

8
00:00:17,005 --> 00:00:20,007
-You're late.
-Yes, Paris was lovely, thank you!

9
00:00:25,948 --> 00:00:27,715
Who the hell is this?

10
00:00:31,787 --> 00:00:34,589
Just 'cause that's what I said to you on
your first day.

11
00:00:35,591 --> 00:00:36,757
Remember?

12
00:00:39,962 --> 00:00:41,295
ADAM: Ow!

13
00:00:43,565 --> 00:00:45,533
GWEN: You make a nice strong coffee.

14
00:00:47,436 --> 00:00:50,237
Sorry, couldn't resist. Come here, you!
Good to see you.

15
00:00:52,574 --> 00:00:54,809
Hey, Tosh, you're looking good.

16
00:01:16,632 --> 00:01:19,333
TOSHIKO: Adam, what are you doing
with your personnel file?

17
00:01:19,434 --> 00:01:23,304
Nothing, just finished updating details
of rift activity.

18
00:01:23,405 --> 00:01:27,308
Any idea when this came through?
It's got a low meson energy reading.

19
00:01:27,409 --> 00:01:29,510
No, I'll keep looking.

20
00:01:47,129 --> 00:01:48,429
A year ago today.

21
00:01:48,530 --> 00:01:50,197
-Our first kiss.
-You remembered.

22
00:01:55,270 --> 00:01:56,971
You okay, Owen?

23
00:01:57,072 --> 00:02:00,875
Yes, yes, yes, don't worry about me.
No, no, it's just...

24
00:02:01,910 --> 00:02:05,980
Kissing in work, I wasn't expecting it.

25
00:02:07,883 --> 00:02:09,550
We'll celebrate tonight.

26
00:02:18,393 --> 00:02:19,760
(GROWLING)

27
00:02:20,529 --> 00:02:22,163
Save it.

28
00:02:26,768 --> 00:02:28,169
Jack?

29
00:02:31,506 --> 00:02:33,274
-You okay?
-Yeah, fine.

30
00:02:35,343 --> 00:02:37,712
-Did you miss me?
-Were you gone?

31
00:02:37,813 --> 00:02:38,946
No!

32
00:02:39,047 --> 00:02:40,981
(GWEN GIGGLING)

33
00:02:41,283 --> 00:02:42,683
(SNARLING)

34
00:02:43,185 --> 00:02:47,822
Just doing a quick check, we had rift
activity two days ago,

35
00:02:47,923 --> 00:02:51,625
-but nothing seems to have come through.
-Apart from me!

36
00:02:55,363 --> 00:02:56,430
What's that?

37
00:02:56,531 --> 00:02:59,900
It's a screen cleaner.
I thought you might like it.

38
00:03:00,001 --> 00:03:01,202
Do you like it?

39
00:03:01,303 --> 00:03:04,705
Just what I need. A small rodent looking
at me while I work.

40
00:03:07,609 --> 00:03:09,510
Think I'll call it Owen.

41
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:14,849
He's like a little puppy
bringing her sticks.

42
00:03:14,950 --> 00:03:16,817
When's he gonna realise
he's got no chance?

43
00:03:16,918 --> 00:03:19,520
Love's blind, apparently.
He's idolised her for years now.

44
00:03:19,621 --> 00:03:23,657
Oh, leave him alone. I think it's sweet.
He's happy.

45
00:03:46,281 --> 00:03:47,648
Oh, sorry! I didn't mean
to frighten you.

46
00:03:47,749 --> 00:03:50,484
-How did you get in?
-With a key.

47
00:03:53,388 --> 00:03:56,023
-This isn't funny.
-You stay back, all right? Stay back!

48
00:03:56,124 --> 00:03:59,560
-Gwen, what's going on?
-How do you know my name? Huh?

49
00:04:02,430 --> 00:04:04,398
I know how to use this.
Who are you and what do you want?

50
00:04:04,499 --> 00:04:06,433
You know who I am.

51
00:04:08,770 --> 00:04:14,275
Fine, if you won't tell me, fine.
You stay there. Don't you move.

52
00:04:15,243 --> 00:04:18,813
Jack, yeah, someone's broken
into my flat. He had a key.

53
00:04:18,914 --> 00:04:19,947
He knows my name.

54
00:04:20,048 --> 00:04:23,517
-Yes, because I live here with you.
-Shut it! Shut it.

55
00:04:23,618 --> 00:04:26,120
Yeah, can you hurry, Jack?
He's a nutter.

56
00:04:28,089 --> 00:04:31,025
You have picked the wrong girl
to stalk, mate.

57
00:04:39,067 --> 00:04:40,401
(BUZZER RINGING)

58
00:04:42,304 --> 00:04:43,604
-Gwen...
-Stay there!

59
00:04:48,109 --> 00:04:50,311
-Jack!
-Gwen, it's us!

60
00:04:54,182 --> 00:04:55,683
In here, Jack!

61
00:05:00,422 --> 00:05:02,323
-What's going on?
-You tell me.

62
00:05:02,424 --> 00:05:06,360
Look, he's put photos of us up.
He must have done it

63
00:05:06,461 --> 00:05:07,728
while I was at work.

64
00:05:07,829 --> 00:05:10,764
He's deluded!
He keeps saying he's my boyfriend.

65
00:05:10,866 --> 00:05:13,067
He is. It's Rhys.

66
00:05:13,802 --> 00:05:16,904
-I've never seen him before in my life!
-You've been with him for years.

67
00:05:17,005 --> 00:05:18,505
See!

68
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:21,175
-Give me the gun, Gwen.
-No! He grabbed me, Jack.

69
00:05:21,276 --> 00:05:22,610
Who knows what he was going to do?

70
00:05:22,711 --> 00:05:24,745
How can you say that?
What have you done to her?

71
00:05:24,846 --> 00:05:26,213
-Nothing.
-Oh, come on!

72
00:05:26,314 --> 00:05:28,983
I know what kind of sick games you play.
Pills that make you forget.

73
00:05:29,084 --> 00:05:30,117
Is that what this is, yeah?

74
00:05:30,218 --> 00:05:32,119
Are you phasing me out
so you can have her all to yourself?

75
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:33,687
-Stay away from him.
-We're engaged!

76
00:05:33,788 --> 00:05:36,657
I bought you
the bloody ring you're wearing!

77
00:05:43,665 --> 00:05:45,766
-Why don't you come with me to the Hub?
-Who the hell are you?

78
00:05:45,867 --> 00:05:47,935
-He's one of us.
-We can check you over.

79
00:05:48,036 --> 00:05:50,070
Jack will stay here
and take care of things.

80
00:05:50,138 --> 00:05:51,405
Okay?

81
00:06:00,315 --> 00:06:04,084
Don't let him go. If he comes
after me again, I'll kill him.

82
00:06:10,325 --> 00:06:13,627
Trust me, I didn't do this,
but whatever's happened,

83
00:06:14,863 --> 00:06:16,630
we'll put it right.

84
00:06:18,433 --> 00:06:22,403
Right, well, no signs
of long term damage

85
00:06:22,504 --> 00:06:25,205
as far as I can see.
Or alien intervention.

86
00:06:25,307 --> 00:06:28,542
But I must be missing something.

87
00:06:28,677 --> 00:06:33,080
I'm sorry, but it's a mystery to me
why you can't remember Rhys.

88
00:06:39,321 --> 00:06:42,256
-Is this really necessary?
-She needs to remember.

89
00:06:42,357 --> 00:06:43,824
(SIGHING)

90
00:06:45,026 --> 00:06:46,760
Where did you meet?

91
00:06:46,861 --> 00:06:50,564
At college, fancied her
from the moment I saw her.

92
00:06:50,665 --> 00:06:51,732
(RHYS CHUCKLING)

93
00:06:51,833 --> 00:06:55,502
Not just her looks, you know.
I mean, she is a looker.

94
00:06:56,871 --> 00:06:58,305
Oh, I...

95
00:06:59,107 --> 00:07:00,407
(RHYS GROANING)

96
00:07:00,508 --> 00:07:03,010
JACK: Tell me about your first kiss.

97
00:07:03,111 --> 00:07:05,846
RHYS: Erm, in the supermarket.

98
00:07:05,947 --> 00:07:10,284
I was going to make her spag bol and...
Then I realised, didn't I?

99
00:07:10,385 --> 00:07:14,188
It's got bloody garlic.
Can't kiss a girl with garlic breath.

100
00:07:16,358 --> 00:07:17,891
No, we were in the queue.

101
00:07:17,993 --> 00:07:19,393
Do you remember that?

102
00:07:19,494 --> 00:07:21,095
Sort of. It's like I'm...

103
00:07:23,631 --> 00:07:27,167
I'm seeing what he's saying, but

104
00:07:27,268 --> 00:07:29,636
I don't remember how I felt.

105
00:07:30,839 --> 00:07:34,575
Believe me when I tell you
that that is your fiancé.

106
00:07:35,744 --> 00:07:38,812
Your memory's just playing
tricks on you, that's all. Okay?

107
00:07:40,015 --> 00:07:41,849
Okay.

108
00:07:41,950 --> 00:07:45,986
She starts to laugh,
she calls me Rhys the rant.

109
00:07:46,721 --> 00:07:49,390
And then she kissed me,
right there in the queue.

110
00:07:49,624 --> 00:07:52,026
And I thought then, Jack,

111
00:07:52,861 --> 00:07:57,431
I thought, "I'm going to marry this
bloody mad woman even if it kills me."

112
00:08:05,407 --> 00:08:07,107
TOSHIKO: Worked out
what that thing is yet?

113
00:08:07,208 --> 00:08:11,078
No joy yet. But you should have a look
at the detail, Tosh, it's gorgeous.

114
00:08:11,846 --> 00:08:13,747
Oh, let me get that.

115
00:08:17,318 --> 00:08:18,919
Have you managed to open it yet?

116
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:22,890
No, sorry. I'm not doing very well,
am I?

117
00:08:22,991 --> 00:08:25,092
It's gonna be a long night.

118
00:08:25,193 --> 00:08:30,064
Yes, which is why I brought
some sandwiches!

119
00:08:30,832 --> 00:08:33,734
One for you, and one for me.

120
00:08:34,569 --> 00:08:38,005
Smoked salmon,
that is your favourite, isn't it?

121
00:08:38,106 --> 00:08:40,007
How did you know that?

122
00:08:43,044 --> 00:08:44,845
I'm gonna need a beer.

123
00:08:44,946 --> 00:08:46,680
What, while we're working?

124
00:08:47,615 --> 00:08:50,317
Oh, yeah, of course. Yeah, right.

125
00:08:50,418 --> 00:08:53,053
Relax, kick back, it's a good idea.

126
00:08:53,688 --> 00:08:55,289
Not for me, though, thanks.

127
00:09:12,607 --> 00:09:14,575
Don't leave me, Jack.

128
00:09:16,878 --> 00:09:18,612
You'll be okay.

129
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:34,294
-What was that all about?
-Temporary amnesia.

130
00:09:34,395 --> 00:09:36,697
Owen's checking possible causes. Oh.

131
00:09:41,202 --> 00:09:44,204
Weevil sighting by
the sewer in Rockall Street.

132
00:09:44,305 --> 00:09:48,075
Jack?

133
00:09:48,176 --> 00:09:51,211
-Can you see him?
-Who?

134
00:09:56,584 --> 00:09:59,119
I'll drop you off
and check out the sighting.

135
00:10:03,258 --> 00:10:07,261
I could come with you. It's been a while
since we went hunting together.

136
00:10:08,096 --> 00:10:10,030
I'll be fine on my own.

137
00:10:12,133 --> 00:10:13,967
(DOOR SLIDING SHUT)

138
00:10:17,138 --> 00:10:19,473
Go on. Live a little.

139
00:10:19,574 --> 00:10:21,775
(SIGHING) Well, as it's you.

140
00:10:24,512 --> 00:10:25,946
Thank you.

141
00:10:26,047 --> 00:10:28,482
-Call it a celebration!
-Oh, yes?

142
00:10:31,419 --> 00:10:33,554
Adam and I have been together
for one year today.

143
00:10:35,223 --> 00:10:36,823
Right, right.

144
00:10:37,725 --> 00:10:39,593
A whole year.

145
00:10:39,694 --> 00:10:42,896
My stomach still flips
when he touches me.

146
00:10:42,997 --> 00:10:46,667
I've never known anything like it.
The two of us, we just fit.

147
00:10:46,768 --> 00:10:49,870
-Do you know what I mean?
-Erm...

148
00:10:49,971 --> 00:10:52,439
Not sure I do, no.

149
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:55,809
Oh, don't worry.
You'll meet the right girl one day.

150
00:10:57,679 --> 00:10:59,379
Yeah. Tosh...

151
00:11:00,515 --> 00:11:02,049
Erm...

152
00:11:03,451 --> 00:11:07,321
Erm, do you really think
I look like a rodent?

153
00:11:09,424 --> 00:11:13,093
Come on, we're going to crack this box
even if it kills us.

154
00:11:28,309 --> 00:11:30,711
Come out, come out, wherever you are.

155
00:11:34,215 --> 00:11:35,749
(GROWLING)

156
00:11:37,185 --> 00:11:41,355
Giving me the run around, huh?
You picked the wrong day, my friend.

157
00:11:46,327 --> 00:11:50,030
Get out! Get out, son.

158
00:11:50,565 --> 00:11:52,866
-Dad?
-Run!

159
00:12:04,145 --> 00:12:06,913
Jack? Was it down there? The Weevil?

160
00:12:08,283 --> 00:12:09,650
No.

161
00:12:09,751 --> 00:12:11,585
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

162
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,754
How did you get here?

163
00:12:13,855 --> 00:12:16,356
I came with you Jack, remember?

164
00:12:17,825 --> 00:12:19,726
Yeah, of course.

165
00:12:22,397 --> 00:12:24,231
Are you okay?

166
00:12:26,167 --> 00:12:28,135
Jack, what did you see?

167
00:12:30,672 --> 00:12:32,039
My past.

168
00:12:40,315 --> 00:12:42,616
-If what you say is true...
-It is.

169
00:12:44,419 --> 00:12:46,219
We love each other.

170
00:12:47,922 --> 00:12:50,090
But how could I forget that?

171
00:13:03,204 --> 00:13:04,838
Nothing in.

172
00:13:06,107 --> 00:13:08,775
I was going to take you out for a meal.

173
00:13:12,246 --> 00:13:13,914
(POURING A DRINK)

174
00:13:15,083 --> 00:13:17,951
Didn't want the weekend
to finish, I suppose.

175
00:13:28,129 --> 00:13:30,364
Jack, please. Talk to me.

176
00:13:30,998 --> 00:13:33,934
What about the past?
Is it your childhood?

177
00:13:40,475 --> 00:13:42,976
I've always been here for you, Jack.

178
00:13:43,077 --> 00:13:46,847
From the very beginning. I'm the one
you can confide in, remember?

179
00:13:49,851 --> 00:13:51,985
It was meant to be buried.

180
00:13:52,086 --> 00:13:54,855
I buried the memory over 150 years ago.

181
00:13:55,690 --> 00:13:57,023
Why now?

182
00:13:58,559 --> 00:13:59,893
Well, maybe it's time.

183
00:13:59,994 --> 00:14:02,462
Maybe up till now, your subconscious
was protecting you.

184
00:14:02,563 --> 00:14:04,765
But you can't block out
the past forever.

185
00:14:04,866 --> 00:14:06,933
I can't afford to remember.

186
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:14,141
-Jack, talk to me, please.
-Why?

187
00:14:14,242 --> 00:14:17,878
-I can help, trust me.
-I'm not sure I should do this.

188
00:14:19,247 --> 00:14:23,683
Just tell me what you see.
I can help you. That's why I'm here.

189
00:14:26,888 --> 00:14:28,755
Where are you, Jack?

190
00:14:44,405 --> 00:14:46,006
Boeshane Peninsula.

191
00:14:47,275 --> 00:14:49,609
My home in the 51 st century.

192
00:14:51,212 --> 00:14:54,047
We lived under the threat of invasion.

193
00:14:56,651 --> 00:14:58,785
They came without warning.

194
00:14:59,854 --> 00:15:03,356
We thought they'd pass over us,
like they always did.

195
00:15:07,128 --> 00:15:08,962
But they didn't.

196
00:15:09,063 --> 00:15:11,565
-Not that day.
-Who?

197
00:15:12,433 --> 00:15:15,836
The most horrible creatures
you could ever possibly imagine.

198
00:15:16,671 --> 00:15:18,538
Their howls travelled before them.

199
00:15:18,639 --> 00:15:21,141
Run! Take Gray. Keep him safe!

200
00:15:21,242 --> 00:15:22,642
Take Gray.

201
00:15:23,544 --> 00:15:24,611
Gray?

202
00:15:25,513 --> 00:15:27,214
My little brother.

203
00:15:28,850 --> 00:15:30,283
No, no, Dad. Come with us.

204
00:15:30,384 --> 00:15:34,087
No, I've got to go get your mother. Run!

205
00:15:42,129 --> 00:15:45,131
One minute I was holding his hand.

206
00:15:56,344 --> 00:15:58,278
I don't know when he let go.

207
00:15:58,346 --> 00:16:00,547
Gray? Gray!

208
00:16:02,149 --> 00:16:03,216
Gray!

209
00:16:03,317 --> 00:16:05,986
Gray, where are you? Gray!

210
00:16:06,087 --> 00:16:09,422
One minute his hand was in mine,
I don't know when he let go. I...

211
00:16:09,524 --> 00:16:12,626
I don't think I noticed.
I thought he was there, just behind me.

212
00:16:12,727 --> 00:16:13,727
Gray!

213
00:16:13,828 --> 00:16:18,632
(WEEPING) I retraced my steps.
Hoping that I'd see him again.

214
00:16:20,501 --> 00:16:22,235
Did you find him?

215
00:16:23,638 --> 00:16:24,704
Gray!

216
00:16:24,805 --> 00:16:26,039
I ran all the way home.

217
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:27,908
Where are you, Gray?

218
00:16:28,476 --> 00:16:30,443
Jack, what did you find?

219
00:16:40,021 --> 00:16:41,321
Dad?

220
00:16:44,625 --> 00:16:45,825
No!

221
00:16:47,762 --> 00:16:51,331
Can someone help? Please!

222
00:16:51,866 --> 00:16:54,067
I searched for Gray for years.

223
00:16:54,969 --> 00:16:57,070
-I never found the body.
-It wasn't your fault.

224
00:16:57,171 --> 00:16:59,105
I let go of his hand!

225
00:17:00,875 --> 00:17:03,243
It was the worst day of my life.

226
00:17:05,046 --> 00:17:07,714
It's the last thing I want to remember.

227
00:17:10,952 --> 00:17:13,019
So, according to
the molecular breakdown,

228
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:17,190
this potentially alien complex artefact
is, in fact, made out of wood.

229
00:17:17,291 --> 00:17:20,260
Well, perhaps it fell in the crate
by mistake.

230
00:17:20,361 --> 00:17:22,596
Picked up meson energy
from the other stuff.

231
00:17:22,663 --> 00:17:24,364
Yeah, right.

232
00:17:24,465 --> 00:17:26,967
Oh, yes, sorry, it's a stupid idea.

233
00:17:27,068 --> 00:17:28,501
I thinkJack brought it in.

234
00:17:28,603 --> 00:17:32,772
No, I'm sure Adam found it on
an excavation a few months back.

235
00:17:32,873 --> 00:17:36,676
I'll have a look in the diary.
I like to log the interesting stuff.

236
00:17:36,777 --> 00:17:39,212
You write about artefacts in your diary?

237
00:17:39,313 --> 00:17:40,981
Among other things.

238
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:48,955
So, we are done for the night.

239
00:17:50,324 --> 00:17:51,591
I guess.

240
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:55,261
Everything all right?

241
00:17:56,297 --> 00:17:58,665
Yeah. Just Adam hasn't rung yet.

242
00:17:58,766 --> 00:18:00,200
Ah.

243
00:18:00,267 --> 00:18:01,801
Sure he will.

244
00:18:03,204 --> 00:18:04,738
I know I would.

245
00:18:05,473 --> 00:18:07,207
If it was our anniversary.

246
00:18:07,308 --> 00:18:08,508
(CHUCKLING NERVOUSLY)

247
00:18:08,609 --> 00:18:13,113
I wouldn't disappear.
In fact, I would, cherish you.

248
00:18:13,914 --> 00:18:18,918
-Ah, Owen.
-Yeah, no, no, really, really I would.

249
00:18:19,787 --> 00:18:22,589
In fact, I wouldn't let you
out of my sight, Tosh.

250
00:18:23,591 --> 00:18:25,925
Because I love you.

251
00:18:27,261 --> 00:18:28,461
What?

252
00:18:30,264 --> 00:18:33,566
Yeah, there we are.
I've said it. I love you!

253
00:18:34,201 --> 00:18:38,605
Yes, I always have, actually,
ever since we

254
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:42,442
started working together
and, in fact, I actually ache for you.

255
00:18:42,543 --> 00:18:45,845
Physically, when you're in the room, I
just want to reach out and touch you...

256
00:18:45,946 --> 00:18:47,347
-Owen.
-No, no.

257
00:18:47,448 --> 00:18:49,182
I can't keep this secret any more.

258
00:18:49,283 --> 00:18:51,918
My mum said to me,
"Seize the day," and so I am seizing it

259
00:18:52,019 --> 00:18:56,089
and, you know, I've got
so much love to give you, Tosh,

260
00:18:56,190 --> 00:18:58,925
and, you know, you wouldn't know that
unless I tell you.

261
00:18:59,026 --> 00:19:02,729
So here I am,
telling you that I love you.

262
00:19:02,830 --> 00:19:06,299
You know, I know there's Adam,
okay, but I think,

263
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:09,736
in fact, I know that we would be
amazing together.

264
00:19:10,237 --> 00:19:13,840
If you would only just give it a chance.

265
00:19:18,145 --> 00:19:19,512
Oh, God.

266
00:19:23,350 --> 00:19:24,818
Say something.

267
00:19:27,221 --> 00:19:30,323
That is completely inappropriate.

268
00:19:31,592 --> 00:19:33,059
-Pardon?
-What are you thinking of?

269
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:35,161
-I'm sorry, I just wanted you to know...
-How dare you!

270
00:19:35,262 --> 00:19:36,996
I'm with Adam.

271
00:19:37,098 --> 00:19:39,099
And even if I wasn't,

272
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:42,402
you're not my type, never will be.

273
00:19:48,876 --> 00:19:49,943
Oh.

274
00:19:51,312 --> 00:19:54,447
-Maybe I should be on my own tonight.
-No way.

275
00:19:54,548 --> 00:19:57,751
-What if you forget who you are?
-I know who I am.

276
00:19:58,986 --> 00:20:01,654
It's not just you who's lost something.

277
00:20:03,257 --> 00:20:06,326
-But you remember.
-All you know about me.

278
00:20:06,961 --> 00:20:08,795
You're my girl, my best friend.

279
00:20:08,896 --> 00:20:10,196
(CASHIER CHATTERING ON PHONE)

280
00:20:10,297 --> 00:20:12,232
Suddenly, all that's gone.

281
00:20:13,033 --> 00:20:16,336
-CASHIER: What about her, mate?
-Where's he going now?

282
00:20:16,437 --> 00:20:18,705
He just walked off!
He knows I'm waiting.

283
00:20:18,806 --> 00:20:22,342
Oh, fine. I'll help myself, then!
Here you are, keep the change.

284
00:20:23,043 --> 00:20:24,878
Buy some spot cream.

285
00:20:24,979 --> 00:20:27,313
I'm not coming here again.
It's overpriced.

286
00:20:27,414 --> 00:20:29,048
There's a £1.50 charge
on the cash machine.

287
00:20:29,150 --> 00:20:31,885
It's a bloody disgrace.
Honestly, kids these days.

288
00:20:31,986 --> 00:20:34,521
Don't know the meaning of hard work.

289
00:20:35,389 --> 00:20:37,190
-What?
-Rhys the rant!

290
00:20:38,859 --> 00:20:41,895
Always when you're in a queue
or driving,

291
00:20:41,996 --> 00:20:46,599
or when you're on the phone to one
of those automated phone thingies.

292
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:49,536
Hey, it's okay. It's okay.

293
00:20:55,509 --> 00:20:56,776
Come on, sweetheart.

294
00:21:13,427 --> 00:21:14,894
What's wrong?

295
00:21:16,664 --> 00:21:19,199
My diary.

296
00:21:21,502 --> 00:21:23,036
You're not in it.

297
00:21:24,538 --> 00:21:26,306
Everyone else is.

298
00:21:27,341 --> 00:21:31,945
Why would I leave you out
when you've been here so long?

299
00:21:36,350 --> 00:21:39,319
Like I'm remembering
a man who doesn't exist.

300
00:21:49,363 --> 00:21:51,097
What are you?

301
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:55,368
Cross me and I will fill you
full of fake memories

302
00:21:55,469 --> 00:21:58,838
until your head is on fire,
because that's how I exist.

303
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:02,642
Gwen. What did you do to her?

304
00:22:02,743 --> 00:22:05,078
Memory's a very delicate thing.

305
00:22:05,179 --> 00:22:07,647
Feeding myself in,
wiped other memories out.

306
00:22:07,748 --> 00:22:10,817
It's a side effect of what
I have to do in order to survive.

307
00:22:10,918 --> 00:22:12,719
Jack has to know!

308
00:22:12,820 --> 00:22:14,187
Remember this.

309
00:22:17,391 --> 00:22:19,259
ADAM: I know you didn't mean
to kill her,

310
00:22:19,360 --> 00:22:20,960
you just couldn't stop yourself.

311
00:22:21,695 --> 00:22:22,829
Remember this.

312
00:22:31,505 --> 00:22:33,907
-I didn't do that.
-Oh, yes, you did.

313
00:22:34,375 --> 00:22:36,609
And she wasn't the first.

314
00:22:42,449 --> 00:22:44,984
ADAM: Good old Ianto, loyal Ianto.

315
00:22:46,020 --> 00:22:48,621
Roaming the streets at night for bait.

316
00:22:49,256 --> 00:22:51,224
My diary!

317
00:22:51,492 --> 00:22:56,095
All human record is a lie. You twist it
into what you want to believe.

318
00:22:58,065 --> 00:23:02,435
But we know the rot in your heart.
You crave flesh.

319
00:23:02,536 --> 00:23:06,706
-No. Please!
-Remember it.

320
00:23:06,907 --> 00:23:08,174
(YELLING)

321
00:23:09,343 --> 00:23:11,210
Remember it.

322
00:23:11,312 --> 00:23:15,248
Remember it! Remember it! Remember it.

323
00:23:15,349 --> 00:23:16,616
(SCREAMING)

324
00:23:17,651 --> 00:23:21,054
I help you dump the bodies.
It's me you call.

325
00:23:23,691 --> 00:23:26,993
You know, I forgot what a rush it is,

326
00:23:27,094 --> 00:23:29,295
feeding in the bad stuff.

327
00:23:29,396 --> 00:23:30,797
(WHIMPERING)

328
00:24:04,064 --> 00:24:07,433
Franklin? Franklin, wake up.

329
00:24:07,534 --> 00:24:08,801
(WEEPING)

330
00:24:08,902 --> 00:24:11,738
-Please.
-Mom?

331
00:24:16,610 --> 00:24:19,579
Where's Gray? Where's Gray?

332
00:24:20,681 --> 00:24:23,449
Where is he, son? Where is he?

333
00:24:24,118 --> 00:24:26,886
We were running so fast.

334
00:24:28,055 --> 00:24:30,490
One moment his hand was in mine.

335
00:24:32,893 --> 00:24:37,730
No, not my little boy.
Not my little boy.

336
00:24:39,333 --> 00:24:43,036
Why now?

337
00:24:59,987 --> 00:25:01,754
Anything?

338
00:25:01,855 --> 00:25:04,624
It's still a bit of a blur
but I'm getting there.

339
00:25:06,093 --> 00:25:08,728
That's all we've got really. Memories.

340
00:25:10,297 --> 00:25:13,566
That's what brought us to here.
To this point.

341
00:25:15,035 --> 00:25:17,904
We found it before, we'll find it again.

342
00:25:19,339 --> 00:25:21,007
You know, I...

343
00:25:23,010 --> 00:25:26,312
I always worried that you'd...

344
00:25:27,448 --> 00:25:30,183
That you'd just settled for me,
you know.

345
00:25:31,819 --> 00:25:34,353
'Cause if you met me now, Gwen,

346
00:25:34,455 --> 00:25:36,722
with all that goes on in your life,

347
00:25:38,258 --> 00:25:40,093
could be that you wouldn't look
twice at me.

348
00:25:40,194 --> 00:25:41,727
Don't say that.

349
00:25:51,205 --> 00:25:53,840
-Do you remember that?
-No.

350
00:25:56,009 --> 00:25:58,544
It felt like the first time.

351
00:26:01,648 --> 00:26:03,282
But it was nice.

352
00:26:13,927 --> 00:26:16,596
-I like that.
-I know.

353
00:26:19,399 --> 00:26:21,167
Remind me some more.

354
00:26:28,369 --> 00:26:29,936
IANTO: Jack!

355
00:26:34,776 --> 00:26:36,576
Ianto.

356
00:26:37,979 --> 00:26:39,179
Hey!

357
00:26:40,381 --> 00:26:42,082
What's wrong?

358
00:26:44,452 --> 00:26:46,820
You have to put me in the vaults.

359
00:26:46,921 --> 00:26:50,690
Lock me up. I killed three girls.

360
00:26:52,393 --> 00:26:54,928
-Strangled them.
-Stop kidding around.

361
00:26:55,997 --> 00:26:57,431
I'm serious.

362
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:01,701
I murdered them in cold blood.

363
00:27:03,738 --> 00:27:05,639
I took their bodies...

364
00:27:12,480 --> 00:27:14,581
You have to lock me away.

365
00:27:15,349 --> 00:27:17,451
Before I turn on you!
None of you are safe.

366
00:27:17,552 --> 00:27:21,021
Hey, hey, come here, come here.

367
00:27:22,757 --> 00:27:24,724
What's happened to you?

368
00:27:34,035 --> 00:27:35,836
I'm a monster.

369
00:27:43,511 --> 00:27:45,312
Best lie detector on the planet.

370
00:27:45,413 --> 00:27:48,415
If something's untrue,
the light turns red.

371
00:27:48,483 --> 00:27:49,850
Go.

372
00:27:52,753 --> 00:27:54,087
My

373
00:27:55,790 --> 00:27:58,959
hands on her throat.

374
00:28:05,967 --> 00:28:08,068
And it felt so good.

375
00:28:09,871 --> 00:28:13,039
Squeezing the life out of her.

376
00:28:19,180 --> 00:28:20,947
It reads as truth.

377
00:28:22,450 --> 00:28:24,217
I don't believe it.

378
00:28:25,553 --> 00:28:28,121
Okay, tell me about the second girl.

379
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:31,992
(WHIMPERING)

380
00:28:33,895 --> 00:28:37,964
She tried to get away,
but I was too quick.

381
00:28:42,670 --> 00:28:43,870
Pleading

382
00:28:45,840 --> 00:28:47,240
and I...

383
00:28:48,242 --> 00:28:49,843
I didn't care.

384
00:28:51,312 --> 00:28:53,446
Something in me wants to kill.

385
00:28:54,448 --> 00:28:55,749
No.

386
00:28:56,684 --> 00:29:00,120
This is not you.
Something's changed you.

387
00:29:00,588 --> 00:29:03,356
You're not a murderer.
I'm certain of it.

388
00:29:13,401 --> 00:29:15,268
ADAM: All human record is a lie.

389
00:29:15,369 --> 00:29:18,939
You crave flesh. Remember this.

390
00:29:19,040 --> 00:29:20,440
(IANTO SCREAMING)

391
00:29:22,577 --> 00:29:24,578
A year ago today. Do you remember that?

392
00:29:24,679 --> 00:29:26,112
Do you remember that?

393
00:29:30,685 --> 00:29:32,052
Who the hell is this?

394
00:29:32,153 --> 00:29:35,388
Just 'cause that's what I said
to you on your first day, remember?

395
00:29:39,227 --> 00:29:42,028
Remember? Remember?

396
00:29:42,129 --> 00:29:45,298
Well, I came with you Jack, remember?
Remember. Remember.

397
00:29:45,399 --> 00:29:47,300
ADAM: I can help you.
That's why I'm here.

398
00:29:47,401 --> 00:29:48,835
Remember this.

399
00:29:49,370 --> 00:29:52,639
JACK: Come here, come here.
Just look, look.

400
00:29:52,707 --> 00:29:53,773
Remember it.

401
00:29:53,874 --> 00:29:55,508
(IANTO SCREAMING)

402
00:29:55,610 --> 00:30:00,614
Remember it. Remember it. Remember it.
Remember it.

403
00:30:06,554 --> 00:30:08,755
Where's Adam's blood sample?

404
00:30:16,731 --> 00:30:20,066
-Everything's in order here.
-When was it last updated?

405
00:30:21,402 --> 00:30:23,603
Twenty four hours ago.

406
00:30:40,254 --> 00:30:42,455
(ADAM AND TOSHIKO CHATTERING)

407
00:30:46,193 --> 00:30:47,761
Oh!

408
00:30:55,336 --> 00:30:59,339
-Owen.
-About last night, it was selfish of me.

409
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:02,942
-Owen, I think the world of you.
-I know. I'm really sorry.

410
00:31:03,044 --> 00:31:04,978
I just don't want to
jeopardise our friendship.

411
00:31:05,079 --> 00:31:07,747
The most important thing
is that you're happy.

412
00:31:08,649 --> 00:31:09,949
Thank you.

413
00:31:10,718 --> 00:31:12,385
Tosh...

414
00:31:12,486 --> 00:31:16,456
You are... You are happy with Adam,
aren't you?

415
00:31:17,158 --> 00:31:20,393
-Completely.
-Okay.

416
00:31:24,632 --> 00:31:27,167
-Hey.
-Hey, how are you today?

417
00:31:27,268 --> 00:31:29,903
Erm, things are coming back slowly.

418
00:31:30,004 --> 00:31:31,504
Rhys thought I shouldn't come
into work but...

419
00:31:31,605 --> 00:31:35,608
Hey, we'll look after you.
You just have to give yourself time.

420
00:31:35,710 --> 00:31:38,144
Come on, group hug.

421
00:31:39,447 --> 00:31:41,114
(GIGGLING)

422
00:31:46,187 --> 00:31:48,188
Hey, Ianto, come here.

423
00:31:51,192 --> 00:31:53,026
You all right, mate?

424
00:31:55,262 --> 00:31:57,597
Listen, I could murder a coffee.

425
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:08,641
Talk to me, Adam.
If that's even your name.

426
00:32:10,644 --> 00:32:12,345
-What?
-What are you doing, Jack?

427
00:32:12,446 --> 00:32:13,947
He's not who you think he is.

428
00:32:14,048 --> 00:32:16,282
He's been feeding himself
into our memories by touch.

429
00:32:16,384 --> 00:32:19,786
-Is this some kind of sick joke?
-He didn't exist until two days ago.

430
00:32:19,887 --> 00:32:21,654
Can somebody tell me
what's going on here, please?

431
00:32:21,756 --> 00:32:24,524
Jack, we've known him for years.
He's part of the team.

432
00:32:24,625 --> 00:32:26,626
-No. He just made you think that.
-Come on, Jack.

433
00:32:26,727 --> 00:32:29,229
Ah, you don't get to me like that.

434
00:32:29,330 --> 00:32:31,664
Jack, you know me.
You recruited me three years ago.

435
00:32:31,766 --> 00:32:33,900
All I know is that when
I think of my team, I see you there.

436
00:32:34,001 --> 00:32:37,404
But I don't feel anything for you.
No pride, no warmth.

437
00:32:38,038 --> 00:32:43,109
You, the one who I can confide in,
the one who unburied the dead.

438
00:32:43,210 --> 00:32:45,879
Jack, maybe you've just forgotten him,
like I did with Rhys, yeah?

439
00:32:45,980 --> 00:32:49,849
I should have spotted it then.
That wasn't stress, that was him.

440
00:32:49,950 --> 00:32:53,286
By making us think we know him,
he disturbs our real memories.

441
00:32:53,387 --> 00:32:55,054
I have no idea
what you are talking about.

442
00:32:55,156 --> 00:32:57,757
-I'm taking him to the vaults.
-Jack, this is ridiculous.

443
00:32:57,825 --> 00:32:59,392
JACK: Move!

444
00:33:00,027 --> 00:33:02,395
-No!
-Tosh, that's not gonna help.

445
00:33:02,463 --> 00:33:03,496
It's fine.

446
00:33:03,597 --> 00:33:06,433
I'm just going to lock him up.

447
00:33:07,868 --> 00:33:10,069
-Let him go.
-I'm not going to harm him.

448
00:33:10,171 --> 00:33:13,440
-Why should I believe you?
-Tosh, Tosh, we can talk about this.

449
00:33:13,541 --> 00:33:15,542
Drop the gun, Jack.

450
00:33:16,977 --> 00:33:18,678
Get off me!

451
00:33:18,779 --> 00:33:21,714
This is what you've done to us. Move!

452
00:33:22,950 --> 00:33:23,983
Adam!

453
00:33:29,824 --> 00:33:33,927
Don't kill me. I had to become part
of your memories in order to survive.

454
00:33:34,028 --> 00:33:36,296
-I didn't mean any harm.
-You changed us.

455
00:33:36,397 --> 00:33:40,366
For the better! You didn't remember
who you were. I helped you.

456
00:33:41,035 --> 00:33:43,837
Look at Owen, all his cynicism gone.

457
00:33:43,938 --> 00:33:46,906
He's a different man now.
Selfless, happier.

458
00:33:47,708 --> 00:33:50,677
And Toshiko, too.
She's never been this confident.

459
00:33:52,780 --> 00:33:55,849
How did you come here? Why us?

460
00:33:55,950 --> 00:34:00,587
All of you have such unique memories.
Especially you, Jack.

461
00:34:01,388 --> 00:34:06,025
All those extraordinary memories
you hold. Some hidden, some absent.

462
00:34:06,594 --> 00:34:08,428
Your singular mind.

463
00:34:09,063 --> 00:34:11,030
That's what drew me here.

464
00:34:12,233 --> 00:34:15,268
Good job. It's what we do best.

465
00:34:16,237 --> 00:34:17,437
Wipe out aliens.

466
00:34:17,538 --> 00:34:20,473
You can't shoot me. You made me live!

467
00:34:21,742 --> 00:34:25,078
And you always remember what you killed.

468
00:34:25,179 --> 00:34:26,713
Don't you, Jack?

469
00:34:34,855 --> 00:34:36,923
Our memories define us.

470
00:34:37,024 --> 00:34:40,293
Adam changed those memories.
Changed who we are.

471
00:34:40,394 --> 00:34:42,562
Now I have to help you all go back.

472
00:34:42,663 --> 00:34:46,099
Find a memory that defines you.
Rediscover who you are.

473
00:34:47,801 --> 00:34:51,437
If I'm wrong, he'll still be here
when we've done this.

474
00:34:55,442 --> 00:34:59,012
Let me take you back
to before we all met.

475
00:35:05,019 --> 00:35:08,187
Feel around for anything
that makes you what you are.

476
00:35:09,623 --> 00:35:12,659
The hidden and the forgotten.

477
00:35:13,861 --> 00:35:15,695
Tell me where you are.

478
00:35:26,941 --> 00:35:29,676
GWEN: The college canteen.
Rhys is sitting opposite me,

479
00:35:29,777 --> 00:35:31,411
telling stupid jokes.

480
00:35:31,512 --> 00:35:33,379
RHYS: Where do you find a tortoise
with no legs?

481
00:35:33,480 --> 00:35:35,181
Where you left it.

482
00:35:36,317 --> 00:35:39,385
OWEN: It's my birthday. I'm ten.

483
00:35:40,020 --> 00:35:42,488
Mum spends the whole day screaming.

484
00:35:42,590 --> 00:35:44,324
"I love you because you're my son."

485
00:35:44,425 --> 00:35:46,292
"But that doesn't mean
I have to like you."

486
00:35:46,393 --> 00:35:47,760
TOSHIKO: Maths club.

487
00:35:47,861 --> 00:35:50,330
Something so reliable about maths.

488
00:35:50,431 --> 00:35:52,465
TOSHIKO: Always the right answer.

489
00:35:54,802 --> 00:35:56,436
IANTO: Meeting Lisa.

490
00:35:56,537 --> 00:35:58,271
Falling in love.

491
00:35:58,706 --> 00:36:00,640
Never felt so alive.

492
00:36:01,875 --> 00:36:04,377
OWEN: I turn 16. She packs my bags.

493
00:36:04,478 --> 00:36:08,147
That is the nicest thing
you've done for me in years, Mother.

494
00:36:08,248 --> 00:36:10,483
GWEN: Kissing him in the supermarket.

495
00:36:10,584 --> 00:36:12,452
The look on his face.

496
00:36:12,553 --> 00:36:14,153
TOSHIKO: My first flat.

497
00:36:14,254 --> 00:36:16,089
I don't have a flat warming.

498
00:36:16,190 --> 00:36:18,091
There's no one I want to invite.

499
00:36:18,192 --> 00:36:19,892
IANTO: Losing Lisa.

500
00:36:19,994 --> 00:36:21,928
Like the world had ended.

501
00:36:22,396 --> 00:36:25,098
GWEN: The way he looks at me sometimes.

502
00:36:25,199 --> 00:36:28,134
As if he's scared of what he feels
for me.

503
00:36:28,235 --> 00:36:29,702
I love him.

504
00:36:33,474 --> 00:36:35,708
But not in the way I love you.

505
00:36:37,978 --> 00:36:39,612
Take this.

506
00:36:41,215 --> 00:36:44,617
TOSHIKO: Knowing there has to be more
to life than this.

507
00:36:44,718 --> 00:36:46,686
Knowing I'm special.

508
00:36:46,787 --> 00:36:49,055
Waiting for someone to see it.

509
00:36:53,027 --> 00:36:54,460
I saw it.

510
00:36:56,196 --> 00:36:57,830
(PILL DROPPING)

511
00:37:00,668 --> 00:37:04,971
OWEN: You save one life, 100 lives,
but it's never enough.

512
00:37:07,141 --> 00:37:08,975
Who'll save me?

513
00:37:10,577 --> 00:37:11,911
I will.

514
00:37:19,453 --> 00:37:21,254
IANTO: Coming here...

515
00:37:21,355 --> 00:37:23,356
It gave me meaning again.

516
00:37:26,994 --> 00:37:28,294
You.

517
00:37:39,339 --> 00:37:43,676
You each have a short term amnesia pill,
it'll make you forget Adam.

518
00:37:43,777 --> 00:37:47,413
We have to wipe out the last
48 hours from our memories.

519
00:37:48,115 --> 00:37:50,016
Go back to who we were.

520
00:37:55,689 --> 00:37:57,323
(PANTING)

521
00:38:32,993 --> 00:38:36,028
I'm going to lose so much.

522
00:38:36,263 --> 00:38:38,231
JACK: None of it was real.

523
00:38:40,868 --> 00:38:44,103
He loved me. And I loved him.

524
00:38:44,204 --> 00:38:46,739
It's no different from real memory.

525
00:38:47,908 --> 00:38:50,143
He forced it on you.

526
00:38:52,146 --> 00:38:53,880
You have to let it go.

527
00:39:06,026 --> 00:39:07,627
(SNIFFLING)

528
00:39:19,239 --> 00:39:20,740
Goodbye, Adam.

529
00:39:57,044 --> 00:39:58,978
Just me left.

530
00:39:59,079 --> 00:40:01,881
Jack, I know what it's like
not to exist.

531
00:40:02,850 --> 00:40:05,418
-Please, don't send me back there.
-I have to.

532
00:40:06,520 --> 00:40:08,521
What are you going to do?

533
00:40:09,122 --> 00:40:11,357
This will wipe out the past two days.

534
00:40:11,458 --> 00:40:13,960
Well, you'll still keep
the bad memories.

535
00:40:14,061 --> 00:40:16,696
Because they were always yours.

536
00:40:16,797 --> 00:40:19,198
But what about the good times, Jack?

537
00:40:20,200 --> 00:40:22,802
What about the last good
memory of you and your dad.

538
00:40:22,903 --> 00:40:25,304
-It's lost.
-I can help you find it.

539
00:40:26,173 --> 00:40:28,841
I can take you back there before I die.

540
00:40:32,746 --> 00:40:36,382
-Why would you do that?
-I was in the void for so long.

541
00:40:36,483 --> 00:40:40,052
The colours of this world
almost blinded me, Jack.

542
00:40:40,153 --> 00:40:44,323
It was so beautiful after the darkness
and the stench of fear.

543
00:40:44,424 --> 00:40:47,927
You gave me that.
Let me do this for you.

544
00:40:49,897 --> 00:40:53,599
Come on, you want this.

545
00:41:10,817 --> 00:41:12,551
It's early evening...

546
00:41:14,354 --> 00:41:16,122
Just me and Dad.

547
00:41:16,223 --> 00:41:17,356
(CHUCKLING)

548
00:41:17,457 --> 00:41:20,693
-Oh, no you don't.
-You're out!

549
00:41:21,295 --> 00:41:22,561
Ah!

550
00:41:24,932 --> 00:41:28,434
You know, one day, you're not gonna want
to play with your old dad any more.

551
00:41:28,535 --> 00:41:29,702
Never.

552
00:41:31,338 --> 00:41:34,240
-Are you there?
-Yeah.

553
00:41:36,009 --> 00:41:37,777
Me, Dad and...

554
00:41:37,878 --> 00:41:41,047
-Dad! Mom said I could play, too.
-...Gray.

555
00:41:41,114 --> 00:41:42,648
Hey, Gray!

556
00:41:47,821 --> 00:41:50,189
-All right, son. One more.
-Okay.

557
00:41:52,459 --> 00:41:54,927
Whoa, I'll get it.

558
00:41:56,563 --> 00:41:58,497
I'm running for the ball.

559
00:42:06,406 --> 00:42:08,708
Some other boy is there.
I don't know him.

560
00:42:08,809 --> 00:42:10,142
-Can I play?
-Who are you?

561
00:42:10,243 --> 00:42:11,911
My name's Adam.

562
00:42:12,012 --> 00:42:16,048
Let me play. Before it gets dark.

563
00:42:16,450 --> 00:42:19,018
There's lots of room.

564
00:42:19,119 --> 00:42:21,454
FATHER: Hey, what are you doing?

565
00:42:22,956 --> 00:42:24,991
-Are you all right?
-I just want to play.

566
00:42:25,092 --> 00:42:26,659
-He can play.
-No.

567
00:42:26,760 --> 00:42:29,328
He doesn't belong here.
I don't want him playing with us.

568
00:42:29,429 --> 00:42:31,497
-I'm Adam.
-Don't touch my dad.

569
00:42:31,598 --> 00:42:35,835
Hey, easy. Are you all right, Adam?

570
00:42:36,670 --> 00:42:38,537
Yes, he just doesn't want to share.

571
00:42:38,638 --> 00:42:41,574
Right, well, if you're going to behave
that way, we're going home.

572
00:42:41,641 --> 00:42:42,675
No. What...

573
00:42:42,776 --> 00:42:44,677
-Come on, Gray.
-No!

574
00:42:44,778 --> 00:42:48,014
We don't leave yet.
We play some more, it gets dark.

575
00:42:48,115 --> 00:42:50,549
We light a fire. Mom joins us.

576
00:42:51,418 --> 00:42:53,886
Come on, son. I'll race you.

577
00:42:53,954 --> 00:42:55,388
Race you.

578
00:42:55,489 --> 00:42:56,655
Dad!

579
00:42:58,692 --> 00:43:01,761
You did this. You spoiled it.

580
00:43:02,396 --> 00:43:03,963
I made it happen.

581
00:43:04,097 --> 00:43:06,866
JACK: Dad! Dad!

582
00:43:08,735 --> 00:43:10,336
I love you.

583
00:43:10,437 --> 00:43:13,873
Dad, Gray! Dad!

584
00:43:15,375 --> 00:43:17,943
I want the real memory back.

585
00:43:18,045 --> 00:43:20,112
Then let me live.

586
00:43:20,213 --> 00:43:22,915
That box you found contains
my last good memory.

587
00:43:23,016 --> 00:43:25,684
Of you, your dad and Gray.

588
00:43:26,286 --> 00:43:28,687
You see, I'm a part of it now

589
00:43:28,789 --> 00:43:31,223
and I'll always live
as long as you remember it.

590
00:43:31,324 --> 00:43:33,692
That's why you took me back?

591
00:43:33,794 --> 00:43:37,363
Wasn't it lovely? Playing in the sand,

592
00:43:37,464 --> 00:43:39,465
no one knowing what was ahead.

593
00:43:39,566 --> 00:43:42,568
Your dad laughing. Gray, safe and happy.

594
00:43:51,111 --> 00:43:53,012
I don't want to die.

595
00:43:53,113 --> 00:43:57,083
You take that pill and you will lose
everything I've given you.

596
00:43:57,184 --> 00:43:58,818
Wipe me out now

597
00:43:58,919 --> 00:44:01,087
and you will lose
all your memories of your father.

598
00:44:01,188 --> 00:44:03,823
He will cease to have existed for you.

599
00:44:08,695 --> 00:44:10,162
Goodbye, Adam.

600
00:44:23,844 --> 00:44:25,678
Dad! Gray!

601
00:44:30,584 --> 00:44:33,886
Come back! It wasn't like this!

602
00:44:49,703 --> 00:44:50,903
Dad! Gray!

603
00:45:25,472 --> 00:45:28,374
Jack, how have we lost two days?

604
00:45:28,475 --> 00:45:30,409
-What do you mean?
-IANTO: Lost 48 hours.

605
00:45:30,510 --> 00:45:32,244
None of us can remember a thing.

606
00:45:32,345 --> 00:45:35,181
The system's blank,
the CCTV's been wiped.

607
00:45:35,282 --> 00:45:38,150
What's been going on?
What've we been doing?

608
00:45:41,121 --> 00:45:42,888
I don't know.

609
00:45:42,989 --> 00:45:46,559
Great. That's two days of my life
that I'll never get back!

610
00:45:46,660 --> 00:45:49,228
Looks like Toshiko got herself
a secret admirer, though.

611
00:45:49,329 --> 00:45:50,563
Oh, yeah?

612
00:45:50,664 --> 00:45:53,999
To Tosh, love and apologies, Owen.

613
00:45:54,668 --> 00:45:56,835
They're from you!

614
00:45:56,937 --> 00:46:00,606
In your dreams, Tosh! I think
somebody's winding you up, darling.

615
00:46:00,707 --> 00:46:02,775
No, I don't do flowers.

616
00:46:04,844 --> 00:46:06,979
And I definitely don't do apologies.

617
00:46:28,034 --> 00:46:30,970
-Did you call?
-Found your diary.

618
00:46:31,071 --> 00:46:32,705
Yep, been looking for that.

619
00:46:35,442 --> 00:46:39,945
And for the record,
measuring tapes never lie.

620
00:46:41,982 --> 00:46:44,383
-Hey!
-Yep?

621
00:46:45,085 --> 00:46:47,019
Who's Adam?

622
00:46:47,120 --> 00:46:49,154
Don't know.

623
00:47:49,182 --> 00:47:51,550
JACK: We've got a murder victim
and a survivor.

624
00:47:51,651 --> 00:47:55,154
Both attacked with hypodermics,
both with their medical records wiped.

625
00:47:56,222 --> 00:47:58,123
OWEN: My money's on this stuff
from Marie's blood.

626
00:47:58,224 --> 00:47:59,591
-I had HIV.
-That's impossible.

627
00:47:59,693 --> 00:48:01,460
OWEN: She's so normal, she's abnormal.

628
00:48:01,561 --> 00:48:03,595
We're on the edge
of the greatest discovery in history.

629
00:48:03,697 --> 00:48:05,798
That's got to be worth a few sacrifices.

630
00:48:05,899 --> 00:48:07,900
JACK: We're not dealing with a freak
with a needle fetish.

631
00:48:08,001 --> 00:48:09,034
This is a conspiracy.

632
00:48:09,135 --> 00:48:11,337
OWEN: It's like the body's been turned
back to its factory settings.

633
00:48:11,438 --> 00:48:13,605
JACK: An alien life form is preying
on the human bloodstream.

634
00:48:13,707 --> 00:48:15,174
That's preposterous.

635
00:48:15,275 --> 00:48:16,642
I need a way in there.

636
00:48:16,743 --> 00:48:18,410
JACK: Miss Martha Jones.
